  "content": "<p><?xml encoding=\"UTF-8\"><span class=\"alignnone size-large wp-image-195 jb-aspect-ratio-wrapper\"><span class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-pillar\" style=\"padding-top: 75%\"></span><noscript class=\"jb-noscript\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://assets.fppdesign.com.au/2018/04/portSTATIONkylie-1280x960.jpg\" alt=\"Business cards for Kylie Sturgess\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-img\"></noscript><img alt=\"Business cards for Kylie Sturgess\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-img lazyload fadein\" data-src=\"https://assets.fppdesign.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/28111149/portSTATIONkylie-361x271.jpg\" data-sizes=\"auto\" data-srcset=\"\"><span class=\"jb-aspect-blurred\" style=\"background-image: url();\"></span></span></p>\n<h2>Kylie Sturgess business cards</h2>\n<p>Kylie Sturgess is a Perth based writer, researcher, interviewer, podcaster, nationally and internationally published author and her tango is something to be seen. Kylie needed a business card to match her infectious enthusiam for science, skepticism and critical thinking, so a slick double sided matt laminate business card with a spot vanish on the front, and her beloved Pod Black Cat drawing on the back was created. Purrrfect!</p>\n<hr>\n<p><span class=\"alignnone size-large wp-image-194 jb-aspect-ratio-wrapper\"><span class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-pillar\" style=\"padding-top: 75%\"></span><noscript class=\"jb-noscript\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://assets.fppdesign.com.au/2018/04/portSTATIONdb-1280x960.jpg\" alt=\"Business cards for Deborah Crabtree\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-img\"></noscript><img alt=\"Business cards for Deborah Crabtree\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-img lazyload fadein\" data-src=\"https://assets.fppdesign.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/28111151/portSTATIONdb-361x271.jpg\" data-sizes=\"auto\" data-srcset=\"\"><span class=\"jb-aspect-blurred\" style=\"background-image: url();\"></span></span></p>\n<h2>Deborah Crabtree business cards</h2>\n<p>Local independent writer Deborah Crabtree required a business card which married the professional with her parallel universe &mdash; her loves of bats, fiction writing and things gothic equaled a simple but atmospheric business card. She loves it.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><span class=\"alignnone size-large wp-image-196 jb-aspect-ratio-wrapper\"><span class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-pillar\" style=\"padding-top: 75%\"></span><noscript class=\"jb-noscript\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://assets.fppdesign.com.au/2018/04/portSTATIONnb-1280x960.jpg\" alt=\"Business cards for Nigel Beck\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-img\"></noscript><img alt=\"Business cards for Nigel Beck\" width=\"1280\" height=\"960\" class=\"jb-aspect-ratio-img lazyload fadein\" data-src=\"https://assets.fppdesign.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/28111148/portSTATIONnb-361x271.jpg\" data-sizes=\"auto\" data-srcset=\"\"><span class=\"jb-aspect-blurred\" style=\"background-image: url();\"></span></span></p>\n<h2>Nigel Beck business cards</h2>\n<p>Business entrepreneur Nigel Beck was looking for an iconic look to cover various aspects of his growing clothing business. To present strong, clean branding representing&hellip; n&iexcl;gel.</p>\n",
